{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774505217,"nonce":"YB1jbmIyz1Od4lQDveNkvL8oAzY=","message":"**GPU scaling benchmark results** (jax.checkpoint on Graph scan body)\n\nHardware: 2x RTX 4090 (24GB each), testing on single GPU (CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0)\nConfig: n_replicates=1, hidden_size=180, n_steps=130, batch_size=250\nJAX 0.5.2, Equinox 0.11.12, XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_PREALLOCATE=false\nWarmup: 5 batches, Adversarial: 10 batches\n\n| N concurrent | Peak VRAM | Wall time | Per-run time | Efficiency |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 688MB | 244.4s | 244.4s | 100% |\n| 2 | 1371MB | 247.6s | 123.8s | 197% |\n| 4 | 2738MB | 254.0s | 63.5s | 385% |\n| 6 | 4106MB | 260.6s | 43.4s | 563% |\n| 12 | 8208MB | 349.5s | 29.1s | 840% |\n| 20 | 23452MB | 575.4s | 28.8s | 849% |\n| 24 | 15003MB+ | 631.5s | N/A | OOM (2 of 24 crashed) |\n\nKey findings:\n- VRAM scales linearly at ~688MB per concurrent run with checkpoint enabled\n- Wall time stays nearly constant up to N=6, then degrades modestly at N=12+\n- Max concurrent runs on a single 4090: ~20 (fills 23.5GB of 24GB)\n- Near-perfect GPU utilization up to 6 concurrent runs\n- Checkpoint enables 20x more runs per GPU vs without (estimated ~5-8GB per run without checkpoint)","files":null}]}